ed a  mid-air collision that rains down debris  over albuquerque  stylistically the event coined many of  the elements that breaking bad and  better call saul would be known for with  evocative black and white prologues  flashing forward to the disaster and a  secret message hidden in the episode  titles the wayfarer disaster was also  something that saw goodman milked for  all it was worth wearing a memorial  ribbon on his lapel for the remainder of  breaking bad in the better call cell  finale he's extradited back to new  mexico to stand trial for his many  crimes flying with the u.s marshal  aboard a wayfarer flight later he enters  the courtroom resplendent in a shiny  saul goodman suit complete with a  wayfarer ribbon pinned to the lapel  the ghost of chuck hangs heavy over the  series finale saul's final courtroom  performance has two major callbacks to  his late brother the most explicit comes  as saul torpedoes his plea deal by  admitting that he was not walter white's  unwitting victim but a willing  participant in his criminal empire that  night i saw opportunity  a shot at big money  saul soon finds himself talking about  chuck and the shot cuts to an angle high  above the courtroom behind an exit sign  buzzing with electricity that image is a  reminder of season three's chicanery in  which jimmy proves that chuck's  professed electromagnetic sensitivity  was a psychological condition the meat  of saul's speech in which he turns away  from a self-serving lie and faces the  truth calls to mind jimmy's testimony to  the bar association at the end of season  four there he tearfully invoked the name  of his brother as nothing more than a  con to get reinstated as a lawyer making  a fool of everyone listening including  kim his final performance reverses that  he praises chuck's brilliant legal mind  acknowledges his culpability in the  events that led to chuck's suicide and  reclaims his family name the name's  mcgill  i'm james mcgill  it's all sincere and i